[gd_resource type="AnimationLibrary" load_steps=6 format=3]

; =============================================================================
;  IRONJAW - locomotion clips
; =============================================================================
;  Ironjaw's half of the pair that drives scripts/cpu_movement.gd, consumed
;  through the BlendSpace2D on fighter_cpu.tscn's AnimationTree exactly as
;  kestrel_locomotion.tres is consumed on Kestrel's. Same five clips, same
;  names, same lengths, same loop contract: each one has to be loopable AND
;  has to open and close on the same pose, because a blend can cut in at any
;  phase and none of them is ever played by name.
;
;  DERIVED FROM KESTREL, NOT AUTHORED FRESH. Both rigs expose an identical
;  joint tree under Rig/Hips, so every track path in kestrel_locomotion.tres
;  already resolves here, and every ROTATION track below is byte-identical to
;  its Kestrel counterpart. The two fighters hold the same orthodox stance -
;  left foot lead, hips bladed -10 degrees, rear (right) foot up on the ball,
;  both fists at guard - so sharing the angles is sharing a pose, not forcing
;  one character into another's motion. Ironjaw reads as the heavier fighter
;  because his geometry is heavier, not because his joints turn differently.
;
;  WHAT COULD NOT BE SHARED: Rig/Hips:position. A Godot value track stores an
;  ABSOLUTE local position, not an offset from the bind pose, so Kestrel's
;  1.296 would be written straight onto a rig whose hips belong at 1.46 and
;  would bury Ironjaw 0.11 units - most of a boot - in the floor. Those keys
;  are the only numbers in this file that differ, and they were recomputed
;  rather than nudged. See below.
;
;  THE RECOMPUTATION. The invariant held was the height of the LEAD (left)
;  sole above the floor at every key - the quantity Kestrel's own GROUND
;  CONTACT note is written about. For a leg of thigh a and shin b with thigh
;  pitch t and knee flex k, the hip-to-ankle drop is
;
;      V = a*cos(t) + b*cos(t + k)
;
;  and the sole sits at  hips.y + upperleg.y - V - sole_offset.  Solving that
;  for hips.y against Ironjaw's chain, at Kestrel's sole height, gives every
;  key below:
;
;                     Kestrel          Ironjaw
;    thigh / shin     0.59 / 0.63      0.58 / 0.70   (chain 1.22 vs 1.28)
;    UpperLeg.y       -0.03            -0.04
;    sole below ankle 0.10 (bare)      0.14 (plated boot, welt included)
;    stance hips      1.296            1.405
;
;  Holding the sole rather than copying the drop is what matters: the same
;  angles on a longer chain drop the hips further, so a shared offset would
;  have skated the lead foot on every clip that changes the knee.
;
;  CONSEQUENCES, CHECKED AT EVERY KEY. The lead sole lands within a millimetre
;  of Kestrel's throughout, planted at 0.000 in stance and in both walks. The
;  rear foot is heel-up by design and never plants flat; its sole rides 0.087
;  above the floor in stance against Kestrel's 0.077, i.e. a centimetre
;  further clear, never through it. Hop lift is preserved too - the lead sole
;  reaches 0.034 at the apex of both hops, the same as Kestrel's.
;
;  UNITS. Node3D:rotation value tracks are RADIANS. Everything was authored in
;  degrees and converted; the degree figures are the ones quoted in comments.
;  Hips:position is in arena units (1 unit ~ 0.68 m).
;
;  ROOT MOTION. None, by design - the same contract Kestrel's library keeps.
;  Translation belongs to scripts/cpu_movement.gd, which integrates it and
;  clamps it against the ring-out lines. These clips only ever move the Hips
;  WITHIN the rig, and every one of those offsets returns to its stance value
;  by the end of the loop, so nothing accumulates.
;
;  CUBIC INTERPOLATION (interp = 2) throughout, inherited with the tracks.
;
;  There is no RESET clip: the bind pose already lives in fighter_cpu.tscn
;  and the tree is only ever active at runtime.
; =============================================================================
;  Five looping clips behind the movement in scripts/player_movement.gd. They
;  are consumed through the BlendSpace2D on fighter_player.tscn's AnimationTree
;  and are never played by name, so each one has to be loopable AND has to open
;  and close on the same pose - a blend can cut in at any phase.
;
;  UNITS. Node3D:rotation value tracks are RADIANS. Everything below was
;  authored in degrees and converted; the degree figures are the ones quoted in
;  the comments. Hips:position is in arena units (1 unit ~ 0.68 m).
;
;  THE SHARED STANCE. All five clips are the same orthodox fighting stance with
;  a different motion laid over it: left foot lead, hips bladed -10 degrees,
;  rear (right) foot up on the ball, both fists at guard. Blending any two of
;  them is therefore blending two variations of one pose rather than two
;  unrelated poses, and that is what keeps every point in between readable.
;
;  GROUND CONTACT. A foot's pitch is the SUM of its thigh, knee and ankle x
;  angles - the rig has no IK, so that sum is the only thing holding a sole on
;  the floor. The sole sits 0.10 below the ankle, and straight-legged the hips
;  ride at 1.35 and the sole lands exactly at y = 0. The stance bends the lead
;  knee 34 degrees, shortening the chain by 0.054, so the stance hips drop to
;  1.296. Every planted foot in every key below was placed against that
;  arithmetic and lands within a centimetre of the floor. Change a knee and you
;  must change its ankle and the hips with it, or the fighter skates.
;
;  ROOT MOTION. None, by design. Translation belongs to player_movement.gd,
;  which integrates it and clamps it against the ring-out lines. These clips
;  only ever move the Hips WITHIN the rig - the lateral lean of a hop, the rise
;  and fall of a step - and every one of those offsets returns to zero by the
;  end of the loop, so nothing accumulates.
;
;  CUBIC INTERPOLATION (interp = 2) throughout. Four or five keys carrying a
;  smooth curve read better than the dozen a linear track would need, and they
;  keep this file small enough to edit by hand.
;
;  There is no RESET clip: the bind pose already lives in fighter_player.tscn
;  and the tree is only ever active at runtime.
; =============================================================================

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  IDLE  -  2.6s loop
;  Fighting stance at rest. It sits at the centre of the blend space, so
;  it is what plays whenever the fighter is not moving.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
